\import{base-macros}
\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{Entropy is subadditive}
\taxon{Theorem}
\tag{public}

\p{The joint [entropy](0081) of a collection never exceeds the sum of the individual entropies:
##{H(X_1,\dots,X_n)\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{n} H(X_i),}
with equality iff the #{X_i} are mutually independent.}

\p{Expand the joint entropy by the chain rule, #{H(X_1,\dots,X_n)=\sum_i H(X_i\mid X_1,\dots,X_{i-1})}, and apply [[H7J5]] term by term: each #{H(X_i\mid X_{<i})\leq H(X_i)}. Conditioning on the past can only shrink each term, so dropping the conditioning gives an upper bound.}
